+# Disaster Recovery (DR) Test Plan (PoC)
+
+Objective:
+- Validate failover for critical components: Aurora DB, Keycloak IdP, Slurm head node, evidence S3 access, and core services (registry, optimizer).
+
+Tests:
+1. Aurora failover
+  - Simulate primary outage: force failover (AWS console or CLI), confirm registry reconnects to new writer, verify no data loss for recent commits.
+2. Keycloak HA failover
+  - Bring down 1 Keycloak pod; verify token exchange still works; simulate full region outage by switching to backup IdP endpoint (if configured).
+3. Slurm headnode failover
+  - Cordon one slurm-head pod and drain; verify head autoscaler brings new replica and running jobs resume or requeue per policy.
+4. Evidence S3 & KMS
+  - Rotate KMS key alias, verify services can still upload & decrypt; test access denied for revoked IAM role.
+5. Webhook cert rotation
+  - Run webhook CA rotation script and verify MutatingWebhookConfiguration accepts new CA bundle and webhooks operate.
+
+Postmortem:
+- Collect logs, upload evidence bundle, and complete SME signoff stored at s3://<EVIDENCE_BUCKET>/incidents/<id>/postmortem.json
